## Before/After Examples

### Example 1 (Fintech) - Bad -> Good
```tsx
// BAD: Pages Router with getServerSideProps
export async function getServerSideProps() {
  const accounts = await prisma.account.findMany();
  return { props: { accounts } };
}
```

```tsx
// GOOD: App Router server component
export default async function AccountsPage() {
  const accounts = await prisma.account.findMany();
  return <AccountsView accounts={accounts} />;
}
```

### Example 2 (Healthcare) - Bad -> Good
```tsx
// BAD: No loading or error boundary for patient routes
// app/patients/page.tsx
export default async function PatientsPage() {
  const patients = await prisma.patient.findMany();
  return <PatientsView patients={patients} />;
}
```

```tsx
// GOOD: Add loading and error boundaries in App Router
// app/(dashboard)/patients/loading.tsx
export default function Loading() {
  return <PatientsSkeleton />;
}

// app/(dashboard)/patients/error.tsx
'use client';
export default function Error() {
  return <ErrorState />;
}
```
